message.content:
Fix these UX issues across admin route files. Read each file first before editing. Run `npm run typecheck` after all edits.

## 1. app/routes/app.delivery-rules.tsx — EmptyState bypasses Free plan gate

The EmptyState "Create your first rule" action calls `openCreate` even when `isFreePlan` is true. Fix by showing a different action on Free plan:

Find the EmptyState around line ~416-429 and change the `action` prop:
```tsx
action={
  isFreePlan
    ? {
        content: "Upgrade to create rules",
        url: "/app/pricing",
      }
    : {
        content: "Create your first rule",
        onAction: openCreate,
      }
}
```

Also fix the `<p>` tags inside Banner and EmptyState — replace with `<Text as="p">`:
- Find `<p>` inside `<Banner>` around line 391-394 and replace with `<Text as="p">`
- Find `<p>` inside `<EmptyState>` around line 424-428 and replace with `<Text as="p">`

## 2. app/routes/app.waitlist.tsx — Multiple UX fixes

**A. Fix `<p>` tags in Banner and EmptyState** — replace all `<p>` with `<Text as="p">`:
- Line ~436-440 inside Banner
- Line ~661-664 inside Banner  
- Line ~783-788 inside EmptyState

**B. Fix `<div style>` wrappers** — replace with Polaris `<Box>`:
- Line ~729: `<div style={{ minWidth: "260px" }}>` → `<Box minWidth="260px">`
- Line ~742: `<div style={{ minWidth: "120px" }}>` → `<Box minWidth="120px">`
- Line ~486: `<div key={...} style={{ minWidth: "120px" }}>` → `<Box minWidth="120px" key={...}>`

**C. Add toast feedback for handleStatusChange** — currently has no feedback. Add:
```tsx
const handleStatusChange = useCallback(
  (id: string, status: string) => {
    const fd = new FormData();
    fd.set("intent", "update-status");
    fd.set("id", id);
    fd.set("status", status);
    fetcher.submit(fd, { method: "POST" });
    shopify.toast.show("Status updated");
  },
  [fetcher, shopify],
);
```

## 3. app/routes/app.settings.tsx — Fix misleading button

**A. Change "Export Zip Codes" to "Manage Zip Codes"** — it navigates to the zip codes page, not an actual export:
Find line ~406-408 and change:
```tsx
<Button onClick={() => navigate("/app/zip-codes")}>
  Manage Zip Codes
</Button>
```

**B. Replace error `<Text tone="critical">` with `<Banner tone="critical">`:**
- Find lines ~272-278 (behaviorFetcher error display) and change from `<Text as="p" tone="critical">` to `<Banner tone="critical">`
- Find lines ~308-314 (notificationFetcher error display) and change from `<Text as="p" tone="critical">` to `<Banner tone="critical">`

You need to add `Banner` to the Polaris imports if not already there.

## 4. app/routes/app.delivery-rules.tsx — Fix premature toast

The `handleSave` and `handleDelete` callbacks show toast BEFORE the server confirms success. This needs to be moved to a useEffect. 

Add a useEffect that watches `fetcher.data` and `fetcher.state`:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (fetcher.state === "idle" && fetcher.data) {
    if ("success" in fetcher.data && fetcher.data.success) {
      const action = "action" in fetcher.data ? fetcher.data.action : "";
      if (action === "created") shopify.toast.show("Rule created");
      else if (action === "updated") shopify.toast.show("Rule updated");
      else if (action === "deleted") shopify.toast.show("Rule deleted");
      else if (action === "toggled") shopify.toast.show("Rule status updated");
    }
  }
}, [fetcher.state, fetcher.data, shopify]);
```

Then REMOVE the direct `shopify.toast.show(...)` calls from:
- `handleSave` (remove line with `shopify.toast.show(editingRule ? "Rule updated" : "Rule created")`)
- `handleDelete` (remove line with `shopify.toast.show("Rule deleted")`)

Also keep the modal close and form reset in handleSave, but only when there's no error. Actually, the modal should stay OPEN until the server confirms. Change handleSave to NOT close the modal immediately — let the useEffect close it on success:

In the useEffect, after showing toast, also close the modal:
```tsx
if (action === "created" || action === "updated") {
  setModalOpen(false);
  resetForm();
}
```

And in handleSave, remove `setModalOpen(false)` and `resetForm()`.

## 5. app/routes/app.waitlist.tsx — Fix premature toast for handleAdd

Same pattern. Add a useEffect for toast + modal close on success:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (fetcher.state === "idle" && fetcher.data) {
    if ("success" in fetcher.data && fetcher.data.success) {
      const action = "action" in fetcher.data ? fetcher.data.action : "";
      if (action === "added") {
        shopify.toast.show("Added to waitlist");
        setAddModalOpen(false);
        setNewEmail("");
        setNewZipCode("");
        setNewNote("");
      } else if (action === "deleted") {
        shopify.toast.show("Entry removed");
      } else if (action === "updated") {
        shopify.toast.show("Status updated");
      } else if (action === "accepted") {
        shopify.toast.show("ZIP code accepted and added to allowed list");
      } else if (action === "rejected") {
        shopify.toast.show("Request rejected");
      } else if (action === "deleted-notified") {
        shopify.toast.show("Notified entries cleared");
      }
    }
  }
}, [fetcher.state, fetcher.data, shopify]);
```

Then remove all direct `shopify.toast.show(...)` calls from:
- handleAdd (also remove the modal close and form reset from handleAdd)
- handleDelete
- handleStatusChange (you already added toast here, remove it again since useEffect handles it now)
- handleAccept
- handleReject
- handleDeleteNotified

IMPORTANT: Run `npm run typecheck` after all edits to verify zero errors.

